<% content_for :title, "Child Safety Standards · say one thing" %>
<% content_for :html_lang, "en" %>
<% @hide_bottom_nav = true %>

<article class="min-h-full bg-slate-50 px-5 pb-16 pt-[max(2rem,env(safe-area-inset-top))] text-slate-700">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-8">
      <p class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-indigo-600">say one thing</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black tracking-[-0.045em] text-slate-950">Child Safety Standards</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">Published and effective: August 20, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-10 text-[15px] leading-7">
      <section aria-labelledby="safety-commitment">
        <h2 id="safety-commitment" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">1. Our Commitment</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="font-bold text-slate-950">say one thing</strong>, operated by
          <strong class="font-bold text-slate-950"><%= @privacy_operator_name %></strong>, has zero tolerance for
          Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation (CSAE) and Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM). We prohibit any use of
          our service that sexually exploits, abuses, or endangers a child.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-prohibited">
        <h2 id="safety-prohibited" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">2. Prohibited Content and Conduct</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">The following content and conduct are strictly prohibited:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-rose-500">
          <li>Creating, uploading, storing, requesting, sending, or distributing CSAM.</li>
          <li>Grooming, sextortion, trafficking of a child for sexual purposes, or any other sexual exploitation of a child.</li>
          <li>Soliciting sexual content, sexual activity, or personal contact from or involving a child.</li>
          <li>Sexualizing a child or encouraging, facilitating, or threatening child sexual abuse or exploitation.</li>
          <li>Using voice messages, account information, or any other service feature to facilitate conduct that endangers a child.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-age">
        <h2 id="safety-age" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">3. Age Eligibility</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          say one thing is not directed to children. Users must be at least 18 years old to use the service. A person
          under 18 must not create or use an account. A parent, guardian, or other person who believes a minor is using
          the service may report the account using the contact method below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-reporting">
        <h2 id="safety-reporting" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">4. Reporting a Child Safety Concern</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-5">
          <p class="font-bold text-slate-950">Child safety reporting contact</p>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Email:
            <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-700 underline underline-offset-2" href="mailto:<%= @privacy_contact_email %>?subject=say%20one%20thing%20child%20safety%20report"><%= @privacy_contact_email %></a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Please include the account or conversation involved, the approximate date and time, and enough context for us
          to locate and review the report. Do not download, copy, attach, or forward suspected CSAM. If a child is in
          immediate danger, contact local law enforcement or emergency services first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-response">
        <h2 id="safety-response" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">5. Review and Enforcement</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">When we receive a report or otherwise obtain actual knowledge of a potential violation, we may:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-indigo-500">
          <li>Review the relevant account, conversation, and available records.</li>
          <li>Remove or restrict access to violating content and preserve relevant information where legally permitted or required.</li>
          <li>Restrict, suspend, or permanently terminate accounts involved in prohibited activity.</li>
          <li>Cooperate with lawful requests from law enforcement and child safety authorities.</li>
          <li>Report confirmed CSAM to the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) or the appropriate regional authority as required by applicable law.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-law">
        <h2 id="safety-law" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">6. Compliance with Child Safety Laws</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We comply with applicable child safety laws and regulations and respond to valid legal process. These standards
          apply globally to every say one thing user and to all voice messages, account activity, and other content handled
          through the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-contact">
        <h2 id="safety-contact" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">7. Designated Child Safety Point of Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Google Play, law enforcement agencies, child safety organizations, users, parents, and guardians may contact our
          designated representative at
          <a class="font-semibold text-indigo-700 underline underline-offset-2" href="mailto:<%= @privacy_contact_email %>?subject=say%20one%20thing%20child%20safety"><%= @privacy_contact_email %></a>.
          This representative can explain our review and enforcement procedures and coordinate action when required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="safety-changes">
        <h2 id="safety-changes" class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950">8. Changes to These Standards</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update these standards to reflect changes to the service, applicable law, or child safety best practices.
          Updated standards will be published on this page with a revised effective date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
        For information about personal data handling, see our
        <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, class: "font-semibold text-indigo-700 underline underline-offset-2" %>.
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
